 ## Languages

 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server selects `en` or `ko` from the request’s `Accept-Language` header,
+using q-values (highest first) and accepting region tags such as `ko-KR`.
+Equal weights use header order; unsupported tags, invalid weights, and q=0
+entries are ignored. If no supported preference remains, the server uses
+`LARDER_LANG` (default `en`). All error codes have messages in both languages.
